{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "or-upsert-on-key-2026-10-04",
    "name": "OpenRegister Upsert On A Declared Key",
    "description": "POST /api/objects/{register}/{schema}?_upsertOn=<constraint>, asserted over HTTP (change api-upsert-on-a-declared-key).\n\nWHAT IT ASSERTS: a key nobody holds creates (201); the same key updates that record (200, same uuid); a key two records hold writes nothing and lists both (409); a name that is not a refuse constraint, a missing key value and _upsertOn with _failIfExists are each a 400. Controls: the listing count after the second upsert, and the untouched Z-DUP record.\n\nIt also asserts that configuration.uniqueConstraints survives a schema save, which the upsert depends on.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT ASSERT: the anonymous 401 and the unseen-holder 409 need a second caller; ObjectsControllerUpsertOnKeyTest covers them.\n\nSELF-CLEANING: it creates and removes its own register, schema and objects.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
